joksh is oksh, the portable OpenBSD Korn shell, with "set -o multiline",
which lets the vi and emacs line editors show a long command line on as
many rows of the screen as it needs, as ksh93 does, instead of in a
window that scrolls sideways; and with fixes to both editors.

joksh is written by a robot engineering team: Claude, an AI model made
by Anthropic, managed by Joe Abley.
